  "id": "COMPOUND:32420 - PROTEIN:5872",
  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C is implicated in the regulation of Solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 2A1 through a series of molecular interactions involving Ent-Gloeosteretriol. The evidence suggests that Oblonganoside C acts as a target for Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which in turn modulates the activity of Solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 2A1. This pathway is supported by multiple high-scoring connections, indicating a consistent and robust relationship across three distinct paths. The shared involvement of Ent-Gloeosteretriol as a mediator in all three pathways underscores a potential mechanism by which Oblonganoside C influences the transporter. The presence of a common target, Ent-Gloeosteretriol, and the consistent pathway from Oblonganoside C to Solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 2A1 suggests a mechanistic link that is both biologically plausible and supported by multiple evidence streams. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Ent-Gloeosteretriol as a central node in the regulatory network, with Oblonganoside C serving as a key activator or regulator of this process.",
